13bc|n|The act of irritating, or exciting, or the state of being irritated; excitement; stimulation, usually of an undue and uncomfortable kind; especially, excitement of anger or passion; provocation; annoyance; anger. ; The act of exciting, or the condition of being excited to action, by stimulation; -- as, the condition of an organ of sense, when its nerve is affected by some external body; esp., the act of exciting muscle fibers to contraction, by artificial stimulation; as, the irritation of a motor nerve by electricity; also, the condition of a muscle and nerve, under such stimulation. ; A condition of morbid excitability or oversensitiveness of an organ or part of the body; a state in which the application of ordinary stimuli produces pain or excessive or vitiated action.	a:u9f,118,3;19kp,96,4;19rc,66,5;1v46,57,1;15u7,28,3;1b5y,19,4~19rc,66,5;19kp,96,4;1b5y,19,4;15u7,28,3;u9f,118,3;1v46,57,1	v:1lhg,49,3;bag,42,4~bag,42,4;1lhg,49,3	n:1cam,81,2;qqk,71,5;1v46,67,2~qqk,71,5;1cam,81,2;1v46,67,2
